  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 South Sudan Bilateral Population Movement Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The protracted armed conflict in Sudan, which dates back to 15 April 2023, continues to trigger large scale cross border movements of displaced persons from Sudan to South Sudan, among other neighboring countries. In addition, the recent widespread conflict from December 2024 in Sudan&#x2019;s regions (Blue Nile, White Nile, Sennar) has further worsened the humanitarian situation, thereby increasing population movement into South Sudan both through official and informal routes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This bilateral proposal has been formulated to help address the increasing humanitarian needs, and seeks to provide funding to address critical gaps, thereby strengthening the South Sudan Red Cross (SSRC) response. This proposal aligns with the Federation-wide National Society Response Plan and complements the Sudan Crisis Revised Regional Emergency Appeal (MDRS1001rea). This bilateral response project, dubbed Renk II, is an extension of the first phase that was implemented from 15 February 2024 till 31 March 2025. Renk II will run for a further one-year period from 1 April 2025 till 31 March 2026, with a budget of Eur 1,145, 835.05 (incl 8% AVK/PSR). The plan focuses on key priority sectors to meet the immediate needs in, Emergency Health, Emergency WASH, Mental Health and Psychosocial Support and Protection needs of 53,550 men, women, boys, and girls in Renk until 31 March 2026.</narrative>
  </description>
